# Projects RBAC Platform

Unified Next.js app: UI in `client/`, API under Express mounted at `/api/*`, single entry `server.js`.

## Commands

- `npm run dev` — UI + API on one port (default `3000`)
- `npm run build` then `npm start` — production
- `npm run db:init` — seed admin user/group/permissions
- `npm test` — Jest (components + API)

## Layout

- `client/app/(app)/` — authenticated shell pages (Home, Admin)
- `client/app/(auth)/` — login/register
- `api/` — Express routes, controllers, models, RBAC
- `docs/openapi.yaml` — API contract for Postman

## Hard rules

- Do not start Express and Next as two separate apps for normal work; use root `npm run dev`
- Keep secrets in `.env`; never commit real credentials
- Prefer same-origin API calls (`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=/api`)
- Docker Mongo needs auth in `MONGO_URI` (or `MONGO_ROOT_USER` / `MONGO_ROOT_PASS`)
